config KAL_CMSIS
    bool "Enable KAL CMSIS"
    default y
    depends on !KERNEL_SMP
    help
      Answer Y to enable LiteOS Kernel Abstraction Layer support CMSIS API.

config CMSIS_THREAD_DEFAULT_OFFSET
    int "Priority Shift"
    default 0
    range 0 7
    depends on KAL_CMSIS
    help
      Anchor shift N for the CMSIS <-> LOS priority mapping: the CMSIS
      value (osPriorityNormal + N) maps to the default LOS priority
      (LOSCFG_BASE_CORE_TSK_DEFAULT_PRIO). Larger N makes the whole
      scale more urgent but shrinks the valid low-end CMSIS domain;
      the upper bound keeps osPriorityHigh mapped to the highest
      usable LOS priority.
